WEBVTT

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.130
<i>- New target detected.
- Ship ahead! The bow is facing us.</i>

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.760
Going by the bridge's shape,
it may be the Musashi!

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.910
W-What should we do? Evade it?

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:01.410
F-Fire? Although we'll be
in trouble if they hit us.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:03.910
The Musashi.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.370
Captain, we're well within their range!

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.880
If we get hit once, we'll be helpless.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.050
L-Left full rudder.
340 degrees, steady as she goes!

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.470
Left full rudder.
340 degrees, steady as she goes!

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.680
<i>The target is 13 miles away.</i>

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.310
13 miles? They shouldn't be that close.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.650
It's not... the Musashi?

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.780
Twin-mounted main battery... Kongou-class!

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:39.910
<i>Kongou-class, 30 degrees to starboard,
azimuth 70 degrees to starboard.</i>

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.320
<i>Maintaining its course!</i>

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.540
That's our school's Hiei?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:47.210
Y102_HIEI
 Y118_MUSASHI

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.500
From afar, it looks just like the Musashi.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:54.170
But the size is very different, which is probably
why Ms. Noma got the distance wrong.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.090
To find the missing Hiei in a place like this.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.770
Contact the school with
the Hiei’s position and course.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.770
I-I know, I know.

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:09.270
- The Hiei is firing!
- What?

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.900
Full speed! Left full rudder!

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.150
Left full rudder!

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.660
What are the school's instructions?

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.160
They requested Blue Mermaid deployment.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:30.210
They'll arrive in four hours. Until then, we
should continue to monitor the Hiei if possible.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:34.000
However, safety of the Harekaze
is the first priority.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.420
That's not where you do your business!

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.430
Rin, put some distance between us and
then go around until we're behind the Hiei.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.600
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.190
Since they fired on us, maybe
they have that virus on board, too?

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.150
Yeah. I think they've been infected.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.570
Just like the Musashi.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.360
Wait!

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:06.200
If the Hiei keeps its course at this speed,
it'll arrive at Chuuk Lagoon in three hours!

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.460
Chuuk. That's...

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.090
Yes. There are over 10,000 residents.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:22.430
Additionally, it's a marine traffic hub with
about 1,000 ships going through every day.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.680
And the Blue Mermaids
will get here in four hours.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.720
Very unlikely that they'll arrive in time.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.600
If that infection spreads,
it'll become a serious situation.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.100
We have to stop them.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.060
Any specific ideas?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.110
If we can draw their attention and get them
off course towards Chuuk.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.450
Compared to following them, the danger
of taking a hit becomes much greater.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.740
Do you still want to proceed?

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:53.620
Yeah. We're faster than them, so I think
we'll make it through somehow.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.840
Rin, get us out in front, and start zig-zagging!

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.380
Understood!

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.190
PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.070
Excuse me.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:37.210
Since you've come here,
it must be something serious.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:38.590
Yes.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:43.010
GENE TRANSFER EXPERIMENT
FOR THE PURPOSE OF MAINTAINING LIFE
IN AN AIRTIGHT ENVIRONMENT
AND ADAPTING TO LOW OXYGEN ENVIRONMENT

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.340
What's this?

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:50.720
The lab ship sank to a depth of 1500 meters.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.390
Couldn't be controlled. Unsalvageable.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:59.860
Is what they thought, but then an active
undersea volcano pushed it to the surface.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.740
Nishinoshima New Islands.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:07.280
This is the rendezvous point
for this year's nautical training.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.990
I filled out paperwork for researchers to be
on board the instructor ship Sarushima.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:18.500
There was a request to research the ecology
of marine life near Nishinoshima New Islands.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:25.800
They were actually a team to collect data from
the experiment ship and then sink it afterwards.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.180
APRIL 14TH

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.100
Its infectious capacity
is greater than we expected.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.770
It may go beyond the Sarushima.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.770
All of us researchers are hospitalized.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:42.520
I never thought this would happen.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.860
How do we report this to our superiors?

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:46.950
We'll be held responsible!

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.410
After that, I investigated on my own.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:51.830
"RATt" ?

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.870
TOTALITARIANISTIC DISEASE

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:58.120
It's the name they gave the organisms that
happened to be born in the undersea plant.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:03.380
These creatures carry a virus
that has an effect on bioelectric currents.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:08.300
That causes the infected
to obey and act to one will.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:15.520
One will... Like an ant or honeybee colony?

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:17.020
Yes.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:21.520
That's why they can remember, but can't
explain the reasoning behind their actions.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:26.150
The bioelectric current is also responsible for
the disruption of nearby electronic equipment.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.360
We got a report from the Harekaze.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:33.580
"This creature is a virus carrier.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.410
I'm sending you the vaccine I created,
so please begin mass production."

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.290
A student developed a vaccine?

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:42.210
Minami Kaburagi is on the Harekaze.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.500
The first genius ever since
the marine medical university started?

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.420
She skipped grades and hadn't done
her marine training yet,

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.260
so she said she wanted to get it done this year.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.100
I did hear she was an eccentric person,

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.060
but I'm thankful for her.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:01.560
"I gather that if the elapsed time is short
after a person is infected,

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:03.860
seawater will negate the virus.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:08.530
However, if more time passes and the virus
spreads throughout the person's body,

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:11.780
I believe only administering
the antibody will be effective."

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:29.710
How long do we have to go at full?
We can't maintain it for that long!

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.510
We're gobbling up oil, too!

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:38.060
Originally, they're cruising range is superior,
and we're continuing unreasonable speed.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.190
If we don't make the next move soon,
we'll hit our limit.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:46.190
Captain, I know how you feel,
but we can't keep this up.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.900
But if we give up...

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:55.160
Then the only thing we can do is stop the Hiei.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.160
Even if that means sinking it.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.540
The Hiei’s broadside armor
is half the thickness of the Musashi's.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.290
Artillery wouldn't work,
but a torpedo would be effective.

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:12.800
Alright, here we go! My era is here!

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.930
Mei Irizaki will humbly sink that ship!

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:20.310
Nobody's ordered you to sink it.
It's hypothetical, if there are no other options.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:20.310
I've been waiting for this moment!
I'll fire! Fire! Fire!

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:26.270
Our classmates are on the Hiei.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:28.480
If something happened to them...

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.740
But at this rate, all we can do
is trail them from a distance.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.240
We have to stop the Hiei without sinking it.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:41.330
The same thing we did with the Spee?

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.710
But even that time, it was impossible!

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.830
Seven secondary armaments
on each side of the ship...

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:51.300
They'll shoot us full of holes
by the time they're in our firing range.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.720
<i>Jeez! You're in the wayzona!</i>

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.050
<i>Ugh!</i>

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.810
<i>And so are you!</i>

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:19.370
We may be able to stop the Hiei!

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.880
<i>Principal, we're getting a transmission
from the Harekaze.</i>

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:31.500
<i>I'll put it through.</i>

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:35.510
<i>This is Akeno Misaki,
captain of the destroyer Harekaze.</i>

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:39.050
<i>We are currently monitoring the Hiei,</i>

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:42.510
<i>but we believe its circumstances are the same
as the Sarushima's and the Musashi's.</i>

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:47.100
<i>At this rate, the Hiei is going to
arrive at Chuuk Lagoon in two hours,</i>

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:51.020
<i>so please give us permission to execute
our strategy to immobilize the Hiei.</i>

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:54.650
The Harekaze alone against the Hiei?
And in broad daylight?

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:57.530
It's impossible. Tell them
to withdraw immediately!

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:00.910
FROM: AKENO MISAKI
TO: MAYUKI MUNETANI
SUBJECT: STRATEGY PLAN
ATTACHED: STRATEGY PLAN SCHEMATICS

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:09.040
This is well thought out.
With this, they can certainly stand a chance.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.790
But, it's too dangerous!

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:15.670
We're the only ones in the area.
Please let us do it!

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:20.220
<i>Do you have enough fuel?
All equipment is working properly?</i>

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:21.680
Yes, ma'am. Everything is working.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.970
And the condition of the students?

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.310
<i>No problems.</i>

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.730
Understood. You have my permission.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:32.150
But first, discuss this
with all of your classmates.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:33.520
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.860
Are you sure about this, Mom?

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:44.200
From what I saw, their plan itself
didn't seem reckless. Besides...

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.040
A cat?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:53.130
It was in the Harekaze's report. The cat
that caught the rat didn't get infected.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:58.130
A good wind may be blowing on that ship.

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:00.930
<i>And that's the overview of the strategy.</i>

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:03.760
We have to go that far to stop them?

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:04.970
<i>Well...</i>

00:12:04.970 --> 00:12:07.560
<i>The Hiei is infected with a virus.</i>

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:08.560
What?

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:11.940
Recall the Chief Artillery Officer's
symptoms the other day.

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:16.690
I believe the crew of the Sarushima and
the Musashi are infected with the same virus.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:21.150
The infected can't control
their own will anymore.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:24.120
But I developed an antibody.

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:27.240
So that was an antibody experiment!

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.700
<i>I sent the data to the school.</i>

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:35.210
<i>So if we can stop the Hiei,
the students aboard can be cured.</i>

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:41.010
<i>But if we just let the Hiei go,
the residents of Chuuk may be infected.</i>

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:45.970
If that happens, the infection
will naturally spread to the rest of the world.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.850
I want to help everyone.

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:52.270
The girls on board the Hiei,
and the people of Chuuk, too,

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:54.230
because comrades at sea are all family!

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:58.110
So will you go off on your own again?

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:04.240
No. Everyone needs to work together
to make this plan succeed.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:10.120
But it puts everyone in danger,
so I can't decide it alone.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:11.750
I want to hear your opinions.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:17.130
The Hiei class has all the honor students, right?

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.750
Doesn't it seem a little too impossible for us?

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.760
And it's a big ship.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.760
It was scary with the Musashi, too.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.890
I-I'll do it! I'll do my best!

00:13:30.890 --> 00:13:33.140
The shy Ms. Shiretoko...

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:37.650
- What do you think?
- Aye, aye.

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.730
- I guess I'm in.
- Yeah, let's do it!

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.360
I have no hesitance!

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.240
I'll help, too. I'm part of this ship as well.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:49.700
- Us too!
- After all, the captain saved us.

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:52.410
- Now it's our turn.
- Right?

00:13:55.210 --> 00:14:00.420
The Hiei’s length is 222 meters. Its total width
is 31 meters. I think we can do this.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:04.300
- But if they fire back...
- As long as we go in circular motions.

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:08.300
I'll strive to the best of my ability,
in the name of Marikouji.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:11.430
- Us too!
- We'll do what we can, right?

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.180
Well, I'm sure we'll manage somehow.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.810
I won't let one wave get past me!

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.900
- We need to prepare ourselves.
- It'll be rough, though.

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:25.200
It looks like Macchi is determined too,
so let's do our best!

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:28.410
- What should...
- ...we do?

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:31.660
Anyway, let's cook some rice!

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:32.950
Let's cook some rice!

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:37.830
But this is just crazy. We don't know
if the engine will hold. Right, Maron?

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:42.340
Alright! Let's do this!

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.380
The captain is the divine palanquin!

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:49.220
Simple-minded as she may be, it's the job
of every true Tokyoite to bear that palanquin!

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:52.430
But the Chief Engineer was born
and raised in Chiba.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:55.890
Still, if the Chief Engineer insists...

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.230
Shall we do it?

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:01.150
<i>Ms. Munetani, you think it's impossible, right?</i>

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:09.160
Considering the characteristics of both ships,
I don't think it's impossible.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:12.780
So... would you lend me your strength?

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:14.620
Ms. Munetani...

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:18.040
Okay.

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:23.000
Captain, since we're going to do this,
I'll give my utmost best.

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:29.720
Thank you, everyone.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.300
Yeah.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:37.270
Prepare for combat!

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.520
Captain, look!

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.440
This is incredible.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.780
My motto is to gather more
and newer data than before.

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:48.530
I've been personally gathering them.

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:51.200
It's a big help. Thank you.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.280
Not bad at all.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:58.200
"If I don't show off here,
the stage ain't never coming to me no more!"

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:01.330
"Although it may be the kind of work
that doesn't have a payoff."

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.130
Mei, Tama! Get ready!

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:05.050
- Alright, leave it to me!
- Aye.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:07.300
Captain! I have a prospective course.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.300
Let's take this route.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.010
Rin, please carry it out!

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:16.310
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.180
Impact on the starboard side!

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.140
Left full rudder!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.810
Left full rudder!

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:27.610
Go back!

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.190
Go back!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.030
HAREKAZE

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:36.660
Shiro! Please give torpedo attack instructions!

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:37.790
Got it!

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:41.750
Launch two torpedoes simultaneously
out of the right tube!

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.630
Aim for the Hiei’s port side, but don't hit it.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.710
That'll be tough.

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:50.470
Main artillery! The canons can't go through, so
you can intend to hit the ship when you fire.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:54.220
But hit close to the port side, and
guide the ship slightly to the right.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:55.140
Aye.

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:57.510
Commence fire!

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:10.240
Please proceed down the planned course.
There are no obstacles underwater.

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.780
"This is the showdown."

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:16.620
"'Cuz if you're gettin' aimed at,
you're stronger than the one doin' the aimin'."

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.120
"There's no goin' back!"

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:20.750
I-I think they're gonna hit us!

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:25.540
Fire one torpedo, left and right!

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:28.170
Please, get through!

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:38.640
<i>We led the Hiei into point one!</i>

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:44.640
If we can make it run aground here,
we can stop it without sinking it!

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:48.400
It got through?!

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:52.150
It fired! Left full rudder!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.910
Point-blank shot!
Impact on the rear starboard side!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.280
Any damage?!

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:00.660
<i>Hang in there a little longer!</i>

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.000
Burst valve!

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:07.580
It's dangerous! We can't maintain
this level of output anymore!

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:08.290
I know!

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.920
<i>Are we done yet, Captain?!</i>

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.420
Just give me 10 more minutes!

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:15.680
Alright, but in 10 minutes,
this whole thing's going to break down!

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:22.220
Confirmed! The Hiei went through point two!

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:27.940
Captain! The Hiei made it through
this grounding point, too! What do we do?!

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.020
We're not done. It's not over yet!

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:32.820
But Captain, it's already...

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.700
There's no storm we can't overcome!

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:38.780
Left full rudder!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:55.420
We're back to the same place? It didn't
strand the Hiei the first time around!

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.300
Hime, now!

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:59.930
Roger! Draining ballast!

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:03.140
Tossing out ballast will make us lose stability!

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.680
Rin, full speed!

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:06.310
No way...

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.190
- Please!
- Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:26.660
The Hiei is on the same course as before!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:30.170
Reduce the speed!
We can't hold for much longer!

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.050
<i>Captain, come on!</i>

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:54.980
The Hiei stopped!

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:59.450
Confirmed. The Hiei’s engine has stopped!

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:04.990
Here you go!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:06.870
Delicious!

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.540
The tide was out?

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.210
It's thanks to you, Coco.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:16.250
You had an online nautical chart, so I knew
about the change in depth in realtime.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:21.760
I see. So the tide was out and the water level
was lower than when we first went through it.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.760
You imagined that far ahead.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:26.890
We saved them, didn't we?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.730
Both Chuuk and the Hiei.

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:33.440
I bet our captain can hold her drink.

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.360
That's a strange compliment.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:40.450
Do you think I was a captain there?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.030
Well, like a captain.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:45.200
To some degree.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.250
D-don't tell me...

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:01.800
I'm Mafuyu Munetani of the Blue Mermaids.

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:03.340
You can leave the rest to me.

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:06.350
Shiro, is that you?

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:09.220
Hey, long time no see!

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:12.100
H-Hey, Sis! Stop it!

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.770
I see. They do have the same family name.

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.940
What are you curling into a ball for?

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:20.150
It's been a while, so you need your big sister
to give you a fresh infusion of confidence?

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:21.610
An infusion of confidence?

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:23.410
I don't need it!

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:25.320
Can I ask for one?

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:26.320
Idiot! Don't...

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:28.330
Sure! Leave it to me!

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:30.540
Brace yourself!

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:32.330
Yes, please!

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:34.870
Alright. First, turn to starboard!

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:35.710
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:38.800
Here we go!

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.590
Guts...

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:43.800
infusion!

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:47.010
Guts, guts, guts...

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.720
Guts, guts, guts...

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:53.730
Huh? Wait, why?

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:58.020
These embarrassing actions need
to stay only within the family.

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:01.480
Well, if you're okay with it, then sure.

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:04.150
But the rear-end is everything to a sailor.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:05.860
Stop it!

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:09.080
Has this butt gotten a little soft?

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:10.910
Stop it, Sis!

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:14.580
A butt like this won't be able to ride out
stormy weather at sea!

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:17.080
- Come on now, guts!
- Stop it, I said!

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.170
Guts, guts! One more time, guts!

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:25.010
Episode 8: In a Pinch with the Hiei!

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:21.590
Sis!

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:24.380
I'm sorry, Shiro...
